Section Three
Population Distribution by Age and Sex
3.0 Introduction
This Section highlights the 2022 PHC results by age and sex. The information is critical for
the implementation of national policies and programmes. Moreover, information on age and
sex is essential in the analysis of demographic determinants of population change (fertility,
mortality and migration ). Detailed statistical tables  from national  to council level, are
presented in Section four.
3.1 Age and Sex Structure
Table 3.1 presents the distribution of Tanzania’s population by 5-year age groups and sex.
Similar inform ation is presented in Table 3.2 for Tanzania Mainland and Table 3.3 for
Tanzania Zanzibar. The data depict a young population age structure  for Tanzania, with
42.8 percent of the population aged below 15 years, and 3.8 percent aged 65 years and
above. The pattern is similar for both  Tanzania Mainland and Tanzania Zanzibar
The median age of the Tanzania’s population is 18 years. The results also depict a higher
number of females than males in almost all age groups, except 10-14.
